  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Prospectus Summary",
      "excerpt": "PROSPECTUS SUMMARY The following summary is qualified in its entirety\nby, and should be read in conjunction with, the more detailed information and financial statements and the related notes appearing elsewhere\nin this prospectus. In addition to this summary, we urge you to read the entire prospectus carefully, especially the risks of investing\nin our Common Stock discussed under \u201cRisk Factors,\u201d \u201cBusiness,\u201d and information contained in \u201cManagement\u2019s\nDiscussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\u201d before deciding whether to buy shares of our Common Stock. Overview Hifortune Holdings Inc (\u201cHifortune,\u201d\nthe \u201cCompany,\u201d \u201cwe,\u201d \u201cour,\u201d or \u201cus\u201d) is a holding company incorporated in the State of\nDelaware on June 23, 2026. We conduct our business operations in China primarily through our PRC operating subsidiary, Yingda Jishi (Shandong)\nEnterprise Management Co., Ltd. (\u201cYin",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "USE OF PROCEEDS Our offering is being made on a self-underwritten\nand \u201cbest-efforts\u201d basis: no minimum number of shares must be sold in order for the offering to proceed. The offering price\nper share is $1.00. We estimate that the net proceeds from the sale of the shares offered hereby will be approximately $759,360, assuming\nthe sale of 100% of the shares offered, after deducting estimated offering expenses of approximately $440,640. We intend to use the net proceeds from this Offering\nas follows (assuming the sale of 100% of the shares offered): Business Expansion & Marketing: $303,744; Professional Staff Recruitment:\n$75,936; SEC Reporting & Compliance: $75,936; Technology & Infrastructure: $75,936; General Working Capital Reserve: $227,808.\nThe amounts set forth above and in the table below reflect our estimated offering expenses of $440,640, which we expect to pay regardless\nof the ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "RISK FACTORS An investment in our common stock involves\na number of significant risks. You should carefully consider the following known material risks and uncertainties in addition to other\ninformation in this prospectus in evaluating our company and its business before purchasing shares of our company\u2019s common stock.\nYou could lose all or part of your investment due to any of these risks. Risks Related to Our Business There is substantial doubt about our ability to continue as a going concern, and we will require additional financing that may not\nbe available to us. For the fiscal year ended June 30, 2026, we incurred a net loss of $191,467, compared with a net loss of $148,424 for the fiscal year\nended June 30, 2025, and we used net cash of $5,092 in operating activities. As of June 30, 2026, we had an accumulated deficit of\n$355,787, current assets of $490,839 and current liabilities",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION Dilution represents the difference between the\nOffering price and the net tangible book value per share immediately after completion of this Offering. Net tangible book value is the\namount that results from subtracting total liabilities from total assets.\u00a0Dilution arises mainly as a result of our arbitrary determination\nof the Offering price of the shares being offered. Dilution of the value of the shares you purchase is also a result of the lower book\nvalue of the shares held by our existing stockholders. Our stockholders\u2019 equity as of June 30,\n2026 was a deficit of $218,122. As of that date, no shares of common stock had been issued, and therefore net tangible book value per\nshare is not applicable. After giving effect to the issuance of 10,000,000 shares of common stock on July 5, 2026 (par value $0.10\nper share; subsequently, on September 21, 2026, the par value was reduced ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "DIVIDEND POLICY We have never declared or paid cash dividends\non our Common Stock and do not expect to pay any cash dividends in the foreseeable future. We intend to retain any future earnings to\nfinance the growth and development of our business. Any return on investment in our Common Stock will depend solely on appreciation in\nthe price of our Common Stock. Any future determination to pay dividends will be at the discretion of our Board of Directors. As of the date of this prospectus, there were 10,000,000 shares of\nour Common Stock outstanding, held by 46 holders of record. There is no established public trading market for our Common Stock, we have\nno outstanding options or warrants to purchase, or securities convertible into, our Common Stock, and no shares of our Common Stock are\nbeing publicly offered by selling security holders. Of our outstanding shares, 10,000,000 shares are res",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
